          },
          {
            title: "Cold damage",
            reasoning: "Tropical plants exposed to cold — a freezing windowsill, a cold draught — can go soft and mushy, sometimes overnight.",
            inspect: ["Was the plant near a cold window or in a cold room?", "Did the softness appear after a cold night?"],
            actions: ["Move the plant to a warm, stable spot.", "Trim away fully mushy parts with clean scissors.", "Do not water until the plant shows signs of recovery."],
